{
  "$schema": "amphora.module-audit-receipt.v1",
  "audit_id": "kpi-surface-completeness-v1",
  "authority": "AUDIT_ONLY",
  "authority_ceiling": "REAL_ARITHMETIC",
  "awaiting": [
    "Human/governance decision on whether every module should be required to carry a consolidated audit-verdicts KPI file (the pattern this module's C10 repair established), or whether evidence/audit/ + benchmarks/ are accepted as the canonical record and evidence/phase0/kpis/ is understood to be a curated subset by design.",
    "If the former: 27 other modules need a repair receipt analogous to this module's audit-verdicts-consolidated-kpi.v1.json, each owned by that module's own cron lane."
  ],
  "axis": "governance",
  "campaign_item_id": "W4",
  "does_not_close": [
    "This receipt performs no new coating-physics test and fits no model; it is a structural/reporting-integrity audit of the repo's own signed-receipt tree.",
    "It does not repair any other module's KPI surface -- repairing 27 other modules' evidence/phase0/kpis/ directories is out of scope for amphora-public-corrosion-benchmark and would require per-module PRs owned by those modules.",
    "The negative-finding flag is a conservative substring heuristic on verdict-field text, not a certified semantic classifier; the full per-receipt detail is included so a human or a follow-up audit can re-grade any entry.",
    "No manifest, no signed Phase-0 KPI, and no cross-module file was modified by this run."
  ],
  "headline": "Across 29 modules with an evidence tree, 162 signed verdict receipts exist under evidence/audit/ or benchmarks/, of which 157 (96.91%) are not referenced anywhere in that module's own evidence/phase0/kpis/ surface -- including 51 findings this audit's heuristic classifies as NEGATIVE (refutation/erratum/underpowered/null/inadmissible language in a verdict field). The claim as stated is FALSE for essentially the whole portfolio, not just the module C10 examined. amphora-public-corrosion-benchmark itself now shows 0 unindexed (post-C10 repair), which is used below as a ground-truth sanity check on the detector.",
  "human_review_performed": false,
  "hypothesis_H0": "Each module's KPI surface (evidence/phase0/kpis/) indexes/reflects the signed DSSE-Ed25519-enveloped verdict receipts that exist for it under evidence/audit/ and benchmarks/ (portfolio-wide generalization of the single-module claim C10 already refuted for amphora-public-corrosion-benchmark).",
  "methodology": {
    "determinism": "os.walk() results are sorted at every level; module list is glob-sorted.",
    "indexed_test": "a signed receipt is counted as INDEXED by a module's KPI surface iff its repo-relative path, its filename, or its own sha256 hex digest appears as a substring anywhere in the concatenated JSON (DSSE-decoded where applicable) of every file under that module's evidence/phase0/kpis/. This is the same reference convention used by this module's own repaired KPI (audit-verdicts-consolidated-kpi.v1.json, which lists receipt_path + receipt_sha256 per audit).",
    "negative_finding_heuristic": "a receipt is flagged NEGATIVE iff the JSON-serialized verdict-field dict, uppercased, contains any of a fixed substring marker list: [\"REFUT\", \"FAIL\", \"WEAK\", \"NULL\", \"UNDERPOWER\", \"INSUFFICIENT\", \"NOT_ESTABLISHED\", \"REJECT\", \"VIOLAT\", \"ERRATUM\", \"INADMISSIBLE\", \"ANTI-CONSERVATIVE\", \"ANTI_CONSERVATIVE\", \"STANDING_OPEN\", \"BROKEN\", \"DISJOINT\", \"OVER-BIND\", \"OVER_BIND\", \"ORPHAN\", \"NOT_SUPPORTED\", \"NOT_EVALUABLE\", \"NO_COMPETENT_MODEL\", \"WRONG_SIGN\", \"UNACHIEVABLE\"]. This is a conservative, auditable proxy, not a semantic classifier -- it is expected to have false negatives (negative findings phrased without these tokens) but few false positives, since the markers are refutation/failure vocabulary this codebase's own receipts consistently use (H0_REFUTED, WEAK_OR_NULL, UNDERPOWERED, etc.).",
    "scope": "every amphora-* top-level directory in the repo root",
    "signed_receipt_detection": "a .json file counts as a signed receipt iff it is a dict with either a top-level 'signature' dict containing a 'payload' key, or top-level 'payload'+'signatures' keys (bare DSSE envelope); the base64 'payload' is decoded and parsed as the verdict JSON. Unsigned diagnostics (diagnostic.canonical.json, plain report.json with no signature envelope) are correctly excluded -- they carry no signed verdict to index in the first place.",
    "verdict_field_extraction": "shallow recursive (depth<=3) scan of the decoded payload for dict keys whose lowercased name contains one of [\"verdict\", \"h0_verdict\", \"result\", \"status\", \"outcome\", \"conclusion\"]; values restricted to str/bool/null so structural sub-objects are not stringified wholesale."
  },
  "modifies_manifest": false,
  "modifies_signed_phase0_kpi": false,
  "module_id": "amphora-public-corrosion-benchmark",
  "own_module_sanity_check": {
    "module": "amphora-public-corrosion-benchmark",
    "n_signed_receipts": 4,
    "n_unindexed": 0,
    "note": "This module's own 4 audit receipts were folded into its KPI surface by the prior fire's repair (audit-verdicts-consolidated-kpi.v1.json, campaign item C10). The detector correctly reports n_unindexed=0 here, which is the expected ground truth and cross-checks that the path/sha256 substring-match methodology used portfolio-wide is not systematically over- or under-counting."
  },
